{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions","id":1134165,"title":"what is the rank of sorcerer in the traditions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-26T10:01:24-07:00","id":1134165,"title":"what is the rank of sorcerer in the traditions?","content":"the only one i found is the hermetic order where they can't rise beyond the third degree. most of the rest of the tradition books say&quot;most do not see the difference&quot; so does that mean that a master of ,say the ephemera is considered the same as a dreamspeaker master of spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:17:58-07:00","id":1134172,"title":"","content":"If we're going by the Revised take on things? Each Tradition has its own way of considering Sorcerers. Hermetics have the most formal ranking system, so they have the easiest time slotting them into it. Most Traditions use a much more loose quasi-merit based approach to internal status, so where they fall is is more up in the air. The Dreamspeakers are the ones noted as caring the least, and they have the most minimal internal hierarchy to worry about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:46:53-07:00","id":1134181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134172#post1134172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're going by the Revised take on things? Each Tradition has its own way of considering Sorcerers. Hermetics have the most formal ranking system, so they have the easiest time slotting them into it. Most Traditions use a much more loose quasi-merit based approach to internal status, so where they fall is is more up in the air. The Dreamspeakers are the ones noted as caring the least, and they have the most minimal internal hierarchy to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes but there is also the official rankings used by all traditions when interacting with each other &quot;initiate apprentice disciple adept master&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:54:19-07:00","id":1134184,"title":"","content":"In general, most Traditions and conventions have a formal ranking of, of course, mundane &lt; Sorceror &lt; True Mage. Even if the lines blur and depend on Tradition and Convention, from a sheer standpoint on the things they can achieve at the top tier, Sorcerors are just at an disadvantage there.<br /> That is not to say though, that The biggest Sorcerors are lower than the lowest mage disciple - as I said, the lines blur, and I bet there are several Traditions where a very prominent and able Sorceror can at least get good respect and position - if not past a certain point because of sheer ability True Magick gives you.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics, and the NWO are probably the groups where a Sorceror/Extraordinary Citizen has probably the least ways of becoming an equal to any Mage/Enlightened Scientist.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the one singular Tradition/Convention that puts Sorcerors on literally equal terms...are the Void Engineers. They don't care if you are an enligtened mind, or are using psionics, or whatever. if you pull your weight, if you fight the good fight, and make a mission work.. you deserve as much respect in their eyes as the biggest of Enlightened Scientists. This goes for Sorcerors/Extraordinary Citizen as much as even a mere mundane, non-enlightened, non-extraordinary VE being a goddamn badass hero.<br /> <br /> And you know, that's kind of cool in my eyes. The VE's always have been, in a big ironic twist, the most down to earth of all groups in many aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-26-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T11:56:48-07:00","id":1134210,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't they be considered Consors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T12:13:05-07:00","id":1134215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134210#post1134210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't they be considered Consors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Even plain mortals can become Consors, so it's nothing that is stuck with Sorcerors. And the Revised Edition books of the Traditions and Technocracy doesn't really use the term much when it comes to Sorcerors - it again depends on the tradition, and with Hermes I can definitely see them being put into that kind of official position. With the Choristers too, probably. Less so with Verbena, Dreamspeakers or the Cult of Extacy - the lines blur there again.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy does not have a term for Consors at all methinks - they simply call Sorcerors 'Extraordinary Citizens' regardless of what exact role they actually perform among the individual convention. And as the VEs show, are far from treated as mere 'Citizens'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:12:54-07:00","id":1134230,"title":"","content":"A Dreamspeaker with Master rank in Spirit can do far more than a Dreamspeaker who masters a sorcery path, even Emphera.<br /> <br /> Consors is a term from Ars Magica (also see companion) and it works nicely for 'they are not us mages but more than just a mere minion (grog).'<br /> <br /> I really don't worry about it, but then I consider sorcerers more a sideline imported into Mage from other games. I just figure my OOH characters learned spells as part of becoming truly magical humans and now do things knowing its they who are the magick. Your Mileage May Vary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:23:52-07:00","id":1134235,"title":"","content":"I imagine certain traditions to be less bothered about where Sorcerors fit in to the whole thing than others.<br /> The Ecstatics don't really care at all, as long as you got a good flow going and are constantly pushing your boundaries, you're all right.<br /> <br /> I can also imagine a whole cabal of Virtual Adepts who go on missions and interact almost entirely only on the orders of their well respected leader, who unbeknown to any of them, isn't actually awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T13:58:31-07:00","id":1134250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions#post1134165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only one i found is the hermetic order where they can't rise beyond the third degree. most of the rest of the tradition books say&quot;most do not see the difference&quot; so does that mean that a master of ,say the ephemera is considered the same as a dreamspeaker master of spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It comes down to what a Tradition values. The more they value things like pride and hierarchy the less a sorcerer's status is going to be. The more they value family and humility, the higher they are going to be allowed to stand. The Hermetics, VAs, Technocracy, and maybe Celestial Chorus are going to be very clear on who stands how high in the pecking order. Dreamspeakers. Hollow Ones, Cult of Ecstasy, and Verbena are likely to have a more relaxed view about the lines between sorcerers and mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T18:37:11-07:00","id":1134309,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Traditions, or even singularly within any Tradition, are you going to find a uniform answer. Some may be very rigid, requiring a battery of magical tests to pass. Others, possibly loose and and less defined, while others a political seat.<br /> <br /> If a character has the Resources to keep the Chantry, the Retainers to protect it, the Cult to enforce his will and the Allies and Contacts to put a hurt on his enemies, they might let it slide that he isn't as magically powerful as the next guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T03:54:31-07:00","id":1134428,"title":"","content":"do we know of any canonical cases where offices in the nine traditions are held by sorcerers? i mean the &quot;federal&quot; bureaucracy not within a tradition itsself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T04:30:48-07:00","id":1134436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134184#post1134184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hermetics, and the NWO are probably the groups where a Sorceror/Extraordinary Citizen has probably the least ways of becoming an equal to any Mage/Enlightened Scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you make this distinction for the New World Order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:57:35-07:00","id":1134524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134428#post1134428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do we know of any canonical cases where offices in the nine traditions are held by sorcerers? i mean the &quot;federal&quot; bureaucracy not within a tradition itsself</div> </div> </div> </div>There's that &quot;Tremere was just a sorcerer&quot; meme that gets floated from time to time.<br /> <br /> (Which to me, is complete and utter BS, but I've got a stack of Ars Magica that talks about what he did as a mage instead of basing it on a pissing contest between &quot;Mage-coolness&quot; and &quot;Vampire-coolness&quot; and trying to drill in on the moment of the transition from House to Clan and doing some really counter-intuitive interpolation.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:30:32-07:00","id":1134563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134428#post1134428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do we know of any canonical cases where offices in the nine traditions are held by sorcerers? i mean the &quot;federal&quot; bureaucracy not within a tradition itsself</div> </div> </div> </div>How far down the ladder are you willing to go? There's no canon cases of them holding positions of note, but they are indicated as holding plenty of the functionary offices in places like Horizon. This is generally done to justify the size of the Tradition infrastructure when mages as supposed to be rare.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that canonically, the idea of mages and sorcerers actually being separate things in the eyes of mages is relatively recent. Until the evolution of magic between the end of the Dark Ages and the start of the Sorcerers Crusade era, the lines between &quot;linear&quot; and &quot;dynamic&quot; magic where considerably more blurred. Years of training in what mages in the modern era call linear magic used to actually lead to becoming a full mage for those capable of it. As the Traditions formed, many of them continued to instruct potential recruits the same way as they always did, but Awakenings became more 'random' and individualistic instead of the result of putting recruits through magical training until their full potential revealed itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:44:07-07:00","id":1134576,"title":"","content":"Setting aside the complete lack of any support for linear magic or it's users in M20, the question would also amount to &quot;Who is doing the testing to determine such things and what are they testing for?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you get points for versatility, the dynamic mages are going to get the props, but if the test is about being able to demonstrate specific power benchmarks, then linear sorcerers might do just as well, depending on their specialties (and if they are &quot;on the board&quot; to determine what gets tested, they very well might skew things towards tests that put them on a more even playing field).<br /> <br /> For example, if the Hermetic so many Spheres at Level X, so many at Level Y, actually works out to some sort of demonstration of those levels of power, then an appropriately trained sorcerer might be able to demonstrate appropriately powerful acts of magic to meet the requirements. Mages could keep out the linear mage riff-raff by having the appropriate testing require demonstrating high levels of versatility for each benchmark (not just &quot;manifest X amount of flame&quot; but &quot;manifest X amount of flame...okay, now lightning.... okay now fly....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:56:01-07:00","id":1134585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134576#post1134576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages could keep out the linear mage riff-raff by having the appropriate testing require demonstrating high levels of versatility for each benchmark (not just &quot;manifest X amount of flame&quot; but &quot;manifest X amount of flame...okay, now lightning.... okay now fly....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And given that, in the case of Hermes at least, Forces is a core essential you can bet they will want all sorts of demonstrations of control over Forces - a Linear mage will have trouble there. Now if we take Verbena, and a linear mage with Alchemy, Divination and/or Healing, they might integrate quite well. Of course on the flipside the Verbena aren't too much about structure in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:58:46-07:00","id":1134768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134576#post1134576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mages could keep out the linear mage riff-raff by having the appropriate testing require demonstrating high levels of versatility for each benchmark (not just &quot;manifest X amount of flame&quot; but &quot;manifest X amount of flame...okay, now lightning.... okay now fly....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking to demonstrate use of the Sphere of Time 3 and 4 Effects could also work. Sorcerers can't do those (speeding time and freezing time), as far as I recall.<br /> Or Entropy 2 Control Probability - Sorcerers can't do this, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-30-2017, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:36:58-07:00","id":1134872,"title":"","content":"It all depends on how the test is given.<br /> <br /> If, to be a specific rank in the Order of Hermes, you just have to demonstrate effects that indicate that you have the right aptitude and they don't demand spontaneity, it's entirely possible Sorcerers could make the cut much higher than they are supposed to. Particularly if the person doing the examining is predisposed to grant the rank. Say.... a Flambeau Master asks the Flambeau sorcerer to create flame from nothing, fan the fame he has created to higher levels of heat, etc. Essentially all things a Sorcerer even with the narrow parameters of a Path could do.... The Flambeau Master might be willing to grant status that would, in terms of required versatility, not be warranted. In fact, with their focus (not Focus), I can see Flambeau and perhaps a few other Houses being more than willing to allow Sorcerers to achieve whatever rank they aspire to. If what you want is flame, the dude has flame, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T11:56:07-07:00","id":1134889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134872#post1134872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If what you want is flame, the dude has flame, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But does she or he have flame, lightning <i>and</i> frost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:19:17-07:00","id":1134894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134768#post1134768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking to demonstrate use of the Sphere of Time 3 and 4 Effects could also work. Sorcerers can't do those (speeding time and freezing time), as far as I recall.<br /> Or Entropy 2 Alter Probability - Sorcerers can't do this, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>many mages don't have these either. besides the list of paths given in the books is not supposed to be the end-all of sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:33:01-07:00","id":1135029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134889#post1134889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does she or he have flame, lightning <i>and</i> frost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the point of the post was that flexibility was not being tested because the Flambeau doesn't CARE so long as there is fire-casting ability, the Verditus doesn't CARE so long as a magicked item is the result, and so on. Allowing Sorcerers access to higher ranks because they pass the &quot;minimums&quot;. So, unless someone is going to tattle to the Quaesitors (I'm looking at YOU Bonisagus mageling), some Houses might have sorcerers in higher positions than the carte blanche ruling would have it be. Seriously, the Flambeau want to have to personnel who can burn shit down. If that means some of them can't also fly, well.... they can burn stuff, burn it REAL good, so what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T20:37:44-07:00","id":1135046,"title":"","content":"Ok, there are two scales here: one scale measures how far you've progressed in mastering a Sphere. Here, sorcerers <i>by definition</i> are rated at zero. Now, there may be a sorcerer who has fooled the local mages into thinking that he has Sphere magic, and maybe convince them to confer upon him a title that he did not earn. But similarly, it's possible for, say, an Initiate too pass for a Disciple, at least for a time \u2014 and conversely, a Master could pass himself off as an Initiate if he had reason to. But the Initiate is still an Initiate and the Master is still a Master, even if no one realizes it. Likewise, a sorcerer is always a sorcerer no matter what. Of course, a sorcerer can potentially do things that an Initiate or Disciple can't; and it's possible that sorcery deserves its own scale, one that doesn't necessarily align with the Spheres.<br /> <br /> The other scale is social and/or political in nature, and varies from group to group. It's not so much about how far you've developed your magic as it is about how much authority and responsibilities you have. The Order of Hermes is the most likely to tie the two scales together; but even they have some flexibility that allows a disconnect between how capable you are with the Spheres and how much authority is bestowed on you.<br /> <br /> Also, Consors are a thing in Mage. At least, they were back in Ascension's Right Hand. And yes, a Consor is &quot;not a Mage, but supernaturally gifted&quot;. The Consors in the book included hedge wizards, psychics, faithful, vampires, Bastet, and so on. The book drew a line between them and ordinary companions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T03:00:19-07:00","id":1135110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135029#post1135029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the point of the post was that flexibility was not being tested because the Flambeau doesn't CARE so long as there is fire-casting ability, the Verditus doesn't CARE so long as a magicked item is the result, and so on. Allowing Sorcerers access to higher ranks because they pass the &quot;minimums&quot;. So, unless someone is going to tattle to the Quaesitors (I'm looking at YOU Bonisagus mageling), some Houses might have sorcerers in higher positions than the carte blanche ruling would have it be. Seriously, the Flambeau want to have to personnel who can burn shit down. If that means some of them can't also fly, well.... they can burn stuff, burn it REAL good, so what?</div> </div> </div> </div>as far as the houses of hermes are concerned .. the canonical answer is..FUCK NO!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> hell i believe the second edition tradition book said that they don't even get to vote..let alone hold office","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:35:11-07:00","id":1135247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135110#post1135110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as far as the houses of hermes are concerned .. the canonical answer is..FUCK NO!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> hell i believe the second edition tradition book said that they don't even get to vote..let alone hold office</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, &quot;As long as the rules as they written down are concerned.... &quot; But the black letter law may be full of brightline rules that get ignored whenever they are considered too restrictive or irrelevant or obstructionist to the goals of the organization, particularly one that is broken down into several sub-parts with different methodologies and missions. <br /> <br /> Could the Bonisagus call the Quaesitori in on the Flambeau and Ex Misc. for playing fast and loose with rules on who gets to use what title? Sure. Are they willing to expend the political capital and create the a heaping pile of ill will when they demand re-testing by objective non-invested personnel? Probably not. I mean, if the Flambeau Adeptus defending a Bonisagus's library with liberal applications of flaming destruction is actually a Sorcerer using a magic Path instead of a Mage with Forces, does it really matter if the books are being defended from whatever perfidy threatens them? Do you want to risk having House Flambeau NOT come to your defense because you were pissy and intrusive about they handled their own internal House business?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T13:40:53-07:00","id":1135256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean, &quot;As long as the rules as they written down are concerned.... &quot; But the black letter law may be full of brightline rules that get ignored whenever they are considered too restrictive or irrelevant or obstructionist to the goals of the organization, particularly one that is broken down into several sub-parts with different methodologies and missions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good example of rules being relaxed would be when the Order accepted the use of Technomagic. Then again, Hermetic Technomancers do tend to stay on the lower ends of the foodchain...<br /> <br /> What you're propossing it's no small thing: I doubt that a single Master (or even a group of Masters) can opt that way without dire consequences. Hermetics are notoriously prideful and &quot;by the book&quot; kind of people. The ranks are there to be used by everyone (not just In-House). You will be trying to force other Masters and proud Disciples to aknowledge your Sorcerer's rank. What's going to happen when you force the cherished Disciple of another Master to obey your *lowly* Sorceror?. That's not something to scoff at. Even if no one takes legal actions, Certamen it's assured (both against the master and the student), treachery and scheeming are assured (against both, too). It seems like a dangerous business to me. If the whole of the House was in...well Flambeau IT'S the most powerful (well, at least the most numerous) house, If someone can pull this off with minimal resistence, they can do it. I'm not so sure about Verditus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:05:12-07:00","id":1135316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135256#post1135256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good example of rules being relaxed would be when the Order accepted the use of Technomagic. Then again, Hermetic Technomancers do tend to stay on the lower ends of the foodchain...<br /> <br /> What you're propossing it's no small thing: I doubt that a single Master (or even a group of Masters) can opt that way without dire consequences. Hermetics are notoriously prideful and &quot;by the book&quot; kind of people. The ranks are there to be used by everyone (not just In-House). You will be trying to force other Masters and proud Disciples to aknowledge your Sorcerer's rank. What's going to happen when you force the cherished Disciple of another Master to obey your *lowly* Sorceror?. That's not something to scoff at. Even if no one takes legal actions, Certamen it's assured (both against the master and the student), treachery and scheeming are assured (against both, too). It seems like a dangerous business to me. If the whole of the House was in...well Flambeau IT'S the most powerful (well, at least the most numerous) house, If someone can pull this off with minimal resistence, they can do it. I'm not so sure about Verditus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever run a Hermetic testing for new rank? If so, how did you set it up? Who did it? What were the requirements? What was the politics around it (as in, was is okay for members of others to be involved? To intervene?)? <br /> <br /> Is ANYONE going to call a Flambeau with 5 ranks in laying out hellfire and damnation and call him &quot;lowly&quot; and expect not to get roasted? Flambeau aren't really noted for calm temperment and lots of self-restraint. Especially when, as you point out, Flambeau is big and powerful and acts their in house military for the most part. Is it worth pissing them off for pride? Be good Hermetic and dish and throw shade in private....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:33:27-07:00","id":1135326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134768#post1134768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asking to demonstrate use of the Sphere of Time 3 and 4 Effects could also work. Sorcerers can't do those (speeding time and freezing time), as far as I recall.<br /> <b>Or Entropy 2 Alter Probability - Sorcerers can't do this, as well</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Fortune / Cursing, Divination, Evil Eye, Precognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T21:57:28-07:00","id":1135349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134524#post1134524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's that &quot;Tremere was just a sorcerer&quot; meme that gets floated from time to time.<br /> <br /> (Which to me, is complete and utter BS, but I've got a stack of Ars Magica that talks about what he did as a mage instead of basing it on a pissing contest between &quot;Mage-coolness&quot; and &quot;Vampire-coolness&quot; and trying to drill in on the moment of the transition from House to Clan and doing some really counter-intuitive interpolation.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My stack of Ars magica books highly suggests Tremere was undeserving of a House and only got one because Tytalus said he wasn't going to join unless Tremere got one. Bonsagius wanted their teacher. There's definately a solid undercurrent of Tremere developing things to counteract that hes not as good a mage as the other founders(creating Certamen for example). Of course the GIFT doesn't function at all like Awakening so converting Ars to Ascension is kind of hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T01:49:15-07:00","id":1135373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135326#post1135326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of Fortune / Cursing, Divination, Evil Eye, Precognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Control Probability allows you to get a specific result in a random event. It does not merely grant a winning or losing result. Control Probability allows you to draw a specific card which is cosmetically different from the other cards with the same mechanical effect in the card game. The Path of Fortune (or the Path of Cursing), as far as I understand, can only alter the odds towards a winning or losing result.<br /> <br /> <br /> How would using divination be at all similar to using Control Probability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-30-2017, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:26:39-07:00","id":1135398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135349#post1135349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My stack of Ars magica books highly suggests Tremere was undeserving of a House and only got one because Tytalus said he wasn't going to join unless Tremere got one. Bonsagius wanted their teacher. There's definately a solid undercurrent of Tremere developing things to counteract that hes not as good a mage as the other founders(creating Certamen for example). Of course the GIFT doesn't function at all like Awakening so converting Ars to Ascension is kind of hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my stack of books say that Tremere invented Certamen which wasn't a lowly sorcerer thing (as you said, that distinction doesn't have ANY meaning in either the Ars Magica or DA Mage systems, well except for the poor Mercere), Tytalus was only really good at it because he was bat-shit crazy and took insane chances (which is what the Tylali were as a House until after the Tremere defection and them taking over some of the political ground and attitudes of their ersatz brother House). <br /> <br /> That makes Tremere one of the Founders of the Order in pride of place next to Bonisagus, Trianoma and Diedne for providing the fundamental foundations for the magic and culture of the nascent Order. Which means he beat EVERYONE in his House who challenged him in a House that is founded on the &quot;one who is best gets to take away the power (specifically and notably all the political voice, but not limited to that by any means) and stuff of the loser&quot;. Tremere was the premiere magical jouster and tournament champion of the Order, except for this one dude who would never fight him because they were brothers. (So the issue never got resolved, really, about who was really better... maybe Tremere would have beat Tytalus and discipline would have won out over sheer brilliant bravado. Remember the Order used to say something to the effect of, &quot;Tremere fight better to learn more , Tytalus learn more in order to fight better'). <br /> <br /> And this is in a system where there explicitly are Sorcerers of a sort in House Mercere (and Tremere and his House are never compared to them). <br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, then was the instigator of pretty much every Wizard War and the primary group that profited from each one (including ousting the largest and most powerful House there was, Diedne, right there at the beginning). And, THEN used Certamen as a political weapon came within a hair's breadth of completely taking over the Order. <br /> <br /> Oh and later did this all completely invisibly behind the scenes as he was officially &quot;dead&quot; and was using a set of puppet Primi to run the House from behind the scenes. (Inferred from the fact that there are other listed Primi for House Tremere... the alternative was that he was successfully able to set up a disguise that the Primi of the other Houses were unable to penetrate.) Though Merinita is recorded as the last Founder to disappear/die (into the lands of the Fae) in 1198, Tremere was apparently still going strong somewhere doing lots of things with a better immortality potion than anyone else from 767 onwards. (And would Tremere let ANYONE but himself prepare that potion?)<br /> <br /> Also, was the first Order member to twig to the fact that the essence of magic was changing from the Dark Ages &quot;paradigm&quot; and start the work to do something about it (not holistically, admittedly, but in the same transcendently selfish manner he did everything else). If he wasn't the first, or even the second, he was doing so to a larger and better organized degree than anyone else that the Order is aware of . <br /> <br /> And, after proceeding the lead the effort to recreate magic from the ground up, did pretty much everything he had done in the Order all over again as a vampire. (Oh, after again almost taking over the entire Order and converting them to vampirism.)<br /> <br /> Sure, I guess that could ALL just be nasty, back-bite-y political know-how, but that doesn't really seem likely with all the evidence stacked up. He could just be one of the master of human resource management of all time. (Building the pyramids? Pshaw! That's nothing. More like building Ancient Egyptian culture from the ground up....) But, accomplishing a lot of those things would either need him to trust other people a whole hell of a lot in a House he built up to be both untrusting and untrustworthy. Undoubtedly, he is taking credit for the accomplishments of others along the line, but some of that, most of that, had to be him. <br /> <br /> Almost certainly, the explanation for Tremere's bad wrap is sour grapes in the Order. For him to be THAT good and done THAT much, he's a contender for the Greatest Hermetic of All Time in terms of power application and raw ability. And their greatest for reals traitor as well. Benedict Arnold was one of the greatest generals the Revolutionary Army had, but he's only remembered as a cowardly traitor. Similar traitors get equivalent reputations among those they betrayed. (Judas was the most important disciple before all that 30 pieces of silver business, etc.) The &quot;he wasn't so good, really, that's why he betrayed us&quot; is a typical human response. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:39:39-07:00","id":1135401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135256#post1135256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good example of rules being relaxed would be when the Order accepted the use of Technomagic. Then again, Hermetic Technomancers do tend to stay on the lower ends of the foodchain...<br /> <br /> What you're propossing it's no small thing: I doubt that a single Master (or even a group of Masters) can opt that way without dire consequences. Hermetics are notoriously prideful and &quot;by the book&quot; kind of people. The ranks are there to be used by everyone (not just In-House). You will be trying to force other Masters and proud Disciples to aknowledge your Sorcerer's rank. What's going to happen when you force the cherished Disciple of another Master to obey your *lowly* Sorceror?. That's not something to scoff at. Even if no one takes legal actions, Certamen it's assured (both against the master and the student), treachery and scheeming are assured (against both, too). It seems like a dangerous business to me. If the whole of the House was in...well Flambeau IT'S the most powerful (well, at least the most numerous) house, If someone can pull this off with minimal resistence, they can do it. I'm not so sure about Verditus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are Paths that allow for the creation of magical doo-dads. If the Verditus tests are about what doo-dads you can create, then they might be more interested in the doo-dad than the dude that made the doo-dad.<br /> <br /> The distinction I'm trying to draw is that the materials we read are largely the &quot;Way the Hermetics See Themselves&quot;. After spending time as both an anthropologist and a lawyer and an archaeologist, I know that for pretty much any aspect of any human culture we know about, &quot;The Way People See Themselves&quot; is only tangentially related to &quot;What People Actually Do&quot;. In fact, there is a step in between, &quot;The Way We See Ourselves (But Really, Everyone KNOWS That We Really Do This...)&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, when I see the brightline Rule, that Hermetics NEVER allow a mere Sorcerer past the third grade of initiation, there's no way I don't reflexively think &quot;Yeah, right....&quot; I'm not saying they do it all the time. It's going to be rare and it's not going to happen everywhere. I'm sure House Quaesitor and Bonisagus would NEVER do it. I'm sure that House Quaesitor is supposed to suss such things out, re-test, convene a Tribunal, Brand and/or Censure the person who was in charge of the test and, at the very least, demote the Sorcerer back to a No. 3 and Brand him (but probably worse). But, there is a political cost to doing so to, say, Flambeau (still the House I think it is likely to happen in most often), that in realpolitik the (very small) Quaesitori and the more wordly and less stick-up-their-asses Bonisagi realize isn't worth it. They are going to know that it's stone cold stupid to piss off what is effectively the (large) military branch of the Order who like to strap their grudges to their backs so their hands are free to cast spells of mighty destruction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:36:54-07:00","id":1135486,"title":"","content":"OK... wading back in a bit:<br /> <br /> This whole test thing feels really weird to me.<br /> <br /> 1) Why are there tests beyond just scanning people? I can make a starting level character that, according to M20, can see a character's Avatar. It doesn't seem like you have to rely on tests of ability at all if the Hermetics want to ban Sorcerers from achieving higher rank.<br /> <br /> 2) Certamen alone would out any Sorcerer. A Sorcerer is incapable of manifesting Arete spheres (not having any), and thus can't grab a Gladius to attack with or an Aegis to defend with (and they don't have any ranks in Spheres to empower them if they could). They also wouldn't be able to form a Locus anyway (maybe a Sorcerer with high levels of Mana Manipulation and Tass could get away with this, but there's a lot of judgement calls to make there).<br /> <br /> While Avatar Storm era games might have this be more difficult, it seems like it should be incredibly easy for mages - esp. the Hermetics - to figure out who's a dynamic mage and who's not. All this testing of what you can do is meaningless when you can basically scan someone for what you're looking for. Or at least put them in a Wonder that only works for people with Arete and Sphere ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:00:27-07:00","id":1135527,"title":"","content":"as for tremere the canonical answer is that he was a mighty mage..but not quites as strong as several other of his rank. this does not necessarily mean low spheres/pillars he just probably just wasn't as good a spell inventor as,say goratrix<br /> <br /> also its implied he had a rather weak avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:29:53-07:00","id":1135648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135527#post1135527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as for tremere the canonical answer is that he was a mighty mage..but not quites as strong as several other of his rank. this does not necessarily mean low spheres/pillars he just probably just wasn't as good a spell inventor as,say goratrix<br /> <br /> also its implied he had a rather weak avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, conversely, no avatar at all. Did you mean a rather weak Font?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:42:02-07:00","id":1135652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1134235#post1134235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can also imagine a whole cabal of Virtual Adepts who go on missions and interact almost entirely only on the orders of their well respected leader, who unbeknown to any of them, isn't actually awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be hilarious.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yo man, our team leader is the most 'leet' of the 'leet'. He's so badass he could blow your mind without even a wink at the keyboard.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But dude, he's only a linear mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Uh... what?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:55:01-07:00","id":1135978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135398#post1135398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost certainly, the explanation for Tremere's bad wrap is sour grapes in the Order. For him to be THAT good and done THAT much, he's a contender for the Greatest Hermetic of All Time in terms of power application and raw ability. And their greatest for reals traitor as well. Benedict Arnold was one of the greatest generals the Revolutionary Army had, but he's only remembered as a cowardly traitor. Similar traitors get equivalent reputations among those they betrayed. (Judas was the most important disciple before all that 30 pieces of silver business, etc.) The &quot;he wasn't so good, really, that's why he betrayed us&quot; is a typical human response.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Hermes didn't write the Ars magica books. The undercurrent that &quot;Tremere is a shitty mage who cheats to keep up with real mages&quot; is very strongly in the text. You can give all the explanations you want but its a pretty easy read and its not purely from In character content. Now the GIFT doesn't match up with any form of Mage so using Ars stuff as a basis is pretty way off. But its not out of some sort of crazy Dick waving contest between games alone this comes up.<br /> <br /> Of course the whole &quot;self embrace with a magic potion&quot; ALSO doesn't seem to match up either Pillar or sphere based magic. Of course we also have the story of the the Nagaraja now who apparently did the same thing with protoeuthanatos pillars and foundation so more support that they were doing something right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T19:09:45-07:00","id":1136048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135978#post1135978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Order of Hermes didn't write the Ars magica books. The undercurrent that &quot;Tremere is a shitty mage who cheats to keep up with real mages&quot; is very strongly in the text. You can give all the explanations you want but its a pretty easy read and its not purely from In character content. Now the GIFT doesn't match up with any form of Mage so using Ars stuff as a basis is pretty way off. But its not out of some sort of crazy Dick waving contest between games alone this comes up.<br /> <br /> Of course the whole &quot;self embrace with a magic potion&quot; ALSO doesn't seem to match up either Pillar or sphere based magic. Of course we also have the story of the the Nagaraja now who apparently did the same thing with protoeuthanatos pillars and foundation so more support that they were doing something right.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like one of those arguments where people get to selectively choose what sources they want to use and discard what they want.<br /> <br /> The Ars Magica books I'm referencing aren't current. They are the materials from before Vampire got spawned, back when Mark Rein dot Hagen was in charge and they are the materials which obviously are the fundamentals for the Order of Hermes. As witnessed, by.... Jesus, EVERY-FUCKING-THING about the Order of Hermes. Everything about the fundamentals of the Order was sucked up from those materials. So, toss that what Tremere did in those books along with the names of the Houses, the Code, the names of the Chantries, what was going down at Mistridge, all that irrelevant data. '<br /> <br /> As is often said you are entitled to your own opinions (that those books don't matter), but not your own facts (that they oh so obviously DO)<br /> <br /> Added Caveat:<br /> <br /> One of the key questions is asking WHO is saying Tremere is a sorcerer, crappy mage, sub par in most every way? WOD deliberately obfuscates who the narrator is by having their fluff often told in the first person by unreliable narrators, but as Brucato points out in some of the essays in BOM, even the 3rd person narrator is deliberately unreliable and varies between stating 'This and such is what people think or say&quot; and &quot;This is what is&quot;. And balance is skewed towards the first over the second. Witness how the information about the various Factions are very skewed depending on which Faction's you're reading. And so on. And so on. Fluff is WOD is always about the &quot;perception&quot; of the reporter, whether that reporter is explicit or implicit.<br /> <br /> So, again, WHO is saying Tremere sucks? In M20, MRev, etc. it's the Order that has every reason to vilify him. And those opinions don't even stand up to the light of inspection as stated with regard to, say, how the Massassa War went down and what the results where in the acrimonious divorce of Clan and Order. (The Hermetics seem to think they fared way better than they did. Witness how the Tremere absconded with a lot of the important stuff. In fact, switching lines, look at the &quot;objective&quot; viewpoint (s)of Clan Tremere on the Order of Hermes. As in, very often, &quot;WHAT Order of Hermes? You mean those guys are still around?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Of course, all that with the caveat of a caveat that, depending on the edition and the book in question, there is a fair amout of fluidity to such things. But, really, that adds to the validity of the core points, not detracts from them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":".  To add Caveat 09-01-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T22:38:45-07:00","id":1136094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135978#post1135978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the whole &quot;self embrace with a magic potion&quot; ALSO doesn't seem to match up either Pillar or sphere based magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain why you think it doesn't &quot;match up&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:17:21-07:00","id":1136155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Of course the whole &quot;self embrace with a magic potion&quot; ALSO doesn't seem to match up either Pillar or sphere based magic.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1136094#post1136094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain why you think it doesn't &quot;match up&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, <i>why?</i> . Hermetics had their potions of longevity in DA: Mage. Alchemy always was one of the legs of hermeticism, why wouldn't they use an alchemical potion as an Instrument?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T06:23:50-07:00","id":1136571,"title":"","content":"This is all fascinating but can someone please point to which books that imply that Tremere was subpar in someway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T19:18:58-07:00","id":1136795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1135373#post1135373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Control Probability allows you to get a specific result in a random event. It does not merely grant a winning or losing result. Control Probability allows you to draw a specific card which is cosmetically different from the other cards with the same mechanical effect in the card game. The Path of Fortune (or the Path of Cursing), as far as I understand, can only alter the odds towards a winning or losing result.<br /> <br /> <br /> How would using divination be at all similar to using Control Probability?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Self Fullfilling Prophecy'<br /> <br /> or in more modern terms,<br /> <br /> Heisenberg's Uncertainty Principle<br /> <br /> You may have heard that in Jurassic Park 2. You can't observe something without effecting it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T00:25:14-07:00","id":1136851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1136571#post1136571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all fascinating but can someone please point to which books that imply that Tremere was subpar in someway?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hermetic Traditionbooks tend to present Tremere as sub-par in at least magical theory and creativity. That he relied on magical power and politics (such as trying to solve things by Certamen as often as possible rather than debates or other more academic competitions), which in the Hermetic system is being a &quot;subpar&quot; magus that doesn't embody their ideal of being an enlightened scholar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1134165-what-is-the-rank-of-sorcerer-in-the-traditions?p=1136795#post1136795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heisenberg's Uncertainty Principle<br /> <br /> You may have heard that in Jurassic Park 2. You can't observe something without effecting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important nitpick:<br /> <br /> You're talking about the Observer Effect. In scientific observation, interaction with the subject is vital, but inherently influences the natural behavior of the subject.<br /> <br /> The Uncertainty Principle is that certain aspects of wave and wave-like systems can't be measure precisely and simultaneously. Measuring an electron's speed and position results in inherent uncertainty, because the more precisely you measure one, the more imprecisely you measure the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T09:59:03-07:00","id":1137346,"title":"","content":"tremere being subpar is implied in many books even vampiric ones. for instance every single one great magical feat of the tremere was done by goratrix. tremere however was very good in(Political not academic) debates,extremely charismatic etc. keep in mind that he was only &quot;subpar&quot; in comparison with the very best of the order.<br /> <br /> certamen was purposefully designed by tremere to force other mages to fight &quot;fairly&quot; i.e your avatar rating(the fount IS the avatar, just not very well understood) doesn't help you spend more quint, also certamen is a literal foundation specialty. tremere also made rules and regulation etc in order to keep them from challenging him.<br /> blood treachery also says he was&quot;limited by happenstance&quot; again strongly implying a weak avatar.<br /> <br /> think of him of as gilderoy lockhar from harry potter(albeit overall far more talented and not an idiot) who was only perfect in memory charms and tried to force situations where it could come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}